   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Rule for using als",
     "texto": [
      "«Als» means \"when\", but only for the non-recurring past: **Als ich in Wien war, besuchte ich ein Museum** (when I was in Vienna, I visited a museum).",
      "If the event happened regularly, «als» can't be used; «wenn» is used instead (**immer wenn**)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Structure of the sentence with als",
     "texto": [
      "As a subordinating conjunction, «als» sends the conjugated verb to the end of its clause: **Als ich klein war**. If the subordinate clause comes first, the main clause starts with the verb (inversion): **Als ich klein war, wohnte ich in Berlin**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
